    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d518">

                <pb facs="0999" n="955" xml:id="pg955"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.5/5–1754: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Tomlinson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Department of State
                        </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d518-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1954-05-17T21:00:00+01:00">May 17, 1954—9
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p> Coled 244. Department pass Bruce. Alphand states government will not bring
                    question of fixing date for EDC debate for Committee of Presidents tomorrow and
                    will oppose fixing date if question is raised on grounds prior conditions of
                    Saar and protocol signature are not fulfilled.</p>
                <p>Intentions now are to wait until after extraordinary Socialist Congress is held
                    before asking committee to fix debate. In this way Socialists will be under
                    discipline in committee and in Parliament in setting date. According to Alphand,
                    procedures have approval of Mollet and Teitgen. Alphand mentioned around June 15
                    or June 20 as possible dates for debate assuming Government does not fall and
                    Indochina situation does not deteriorate.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tomlinson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d518-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d518-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated for information to Bonn and London.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
